# ALL.rc — DECLARED exit codes for entries whose CORRECT run exits nonzero.
# Format: name<TAB>rc   ·   blank lines and # comments ignored   ·   rc=0 is the default and is REFUSED here.
#
# ⛔ DECLARED, NEVER INFERRED: classify() refuses to call a nonzero-rc run a PASS unless the
# entry declares that exit code here, so an undeclared nonzero rc is a FAIL and not a silent pass.
ladder__rung23_keyword_and_system_variables_code_exit_value	4
#
# The expected rc is the ORACLE's (Lon 2026-11-05: the expected result is the oracle's exit code, stdout and stderr). simple_output_151 and
# ladder__rung23_keyword_and_system_variables_stlimit_halts_a_loop_body declare nothing: sbl -bf, through util_oracle.sh on the scrip --transpile
# text, exits 0 after the fatal (measured 2026-11-05 on SCRIP 5217bd1e8: simple_output_151 ERROR 243 "function result in nreturn is not name",
# stlimit_halts_a_loop_body ERROR 244; and a fatal at the default &CODE exits 0, after &CODE = 7 it exits 7). The earlier rc 1 lines were declared
# from SCRIP's old one-voice exit 1, never from the oracle. The halt is told from a silent completion by the ref, which is the stdout before the
# fatal: 'before' without 'after'; 1 2 3 14 12 without 'nreturn ok' (cfo 2026-10-23, CEO-1926, Lon in-chat to the cfo: "You should fix any
# incorrect REF files."): NullFn never assigns its own name, so its NRETURN hands back the null string, and the oracle stops there; the old sixth
# line "nreturn ok" was the source header's hand-written expectation, never the oracle's.
